{
  "name": "Caldera",
  "stage": "Vents",
  "summary": "A crater ringed by six vents and a rock rim. The water inside is still, so minerals pool in the basin and the gate cell sits at its centre. The way in is through one of three passes, then across the hot ring between two vents.",
  "pillars": [
    "Thermal topology: the danger is a closed ring, not a point. The player must find the cool gaps between vents.",
    "Still water (no drift) lets minerals pile up inside the ring: the richest water of the stage is in the middle, behind the heat.",
    "The rim passes are chokepoints. Outside the rim is cold, poor and safe; inside is rich and patrolled.",
    "Thermophiles live on the ring where nothing else can follow, so they are prey only for a heat-proof cell."
  ],
  "proposals": [
    "Thermophile trait: a creature that takes no heat damage (and a gene that gives it).",
    "Vent pulse: the six vents flare in turn, so a gap that is cool now is hot a few seconds later."
  ],
